1,2 $ Lamellae brownish to pinkish brown or becoming so with age
1,4 $ Lamellae white, pallid, pale buff or yellowish, not darkening appreciably with age
2,0 $ Pileus pale buff to yellowish or brownish yellow $C. biformis  149. 
2,3 $ Pileus brick color to terra cotta or yellowish brown
3,0 $ Pileus brick color to terra cotta when moist; odor not distinctive $C. inversa  148. 
3,0 $ Pileus yellowish brown; odor of curry $ C. shafferi  151. 
4,0 $ Pileus flesh color to yellowish moist $ C. maculosa  152.
4,5 $ Pileus vinaceous brown, cinnamon, rusty red, ferruginous, tawny moist...
5,0 $ Pileus small (up to 31 mm), vinaceous brown moist; clamp connections absent.. $ C. femoralis 153. 
5,0 $ Pileus medium to large (3-11 cm), rusty red, ferruginous, cinnamon, tawny, orange tan moist; clamp connections present $  C. flaccida 150.
